                "ImageDescription": {
                  "value": "Badi chura is a semi-ground form of shallow-fried Badi/bodi (sun-dried black gram dumpling) that is often mixed with garlic, onion and chilli pepper. It is consumed as a side dish with <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pakhala\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Pakhala\">Pakhala</a> and rice. The dish is a native of Odisha, India and is popular in eastern India.",
                  "source": "commons-desc-page"
                },
