                "ImageDescription": {
                  "value": "<i>Ou khota</i> or <i>Ou khata</i> is a cooked dish made from elephant apple. Elephant apple is cut into long pieces, marinated in turmeric powder and boiled in water, sautéed with <i>poncho phutono</i>/<i>pancha phutana</i> and cooked for some time with a little bit of salt and jaggery, garnished with grated coconut and cooked again for sometime. \n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 150px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_1_-_Elephant_apple_cut_into_long_pieces.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"Step 1: Elephant apple cut into long pieces\"><img alt=\"Step 1: Elephant apple cut into long pieces\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_1_-_Elephant_apple_cut_into_long_pieces.jpg/120px-Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_1_-_Elephant_apple_cut_into_long_pieces.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"90\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_1_-_Elephant_apple_cut_into_long_pieces.jpg/250px-Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_1_-_Elephant_apple_cut_into_long_pieces.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2448\" data-file-height=\"3264\"></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">Step 1: Elephant apple cut into long pieces</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 150px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_2_-_Elephant_apple_boiled_with_turmeric.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"Step 2: It is marinated with turmeric power and boiled in water\"><img alt=\"Step 2: It is marinated with turmeric power and boiled in water\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_2_-_Elephant_apple_boiled_with_turmeric.jpg/120px-Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_2_-_Elephant_apple_boiled_with_turmeric.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"111\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_2_-_Elephant_apple_boiled_with_turmeric.jpg/250px-Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_2_-_Elephant_apple_boiled_with_turmeric.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2448\" data-file-height=\"2643\"></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">Step 2: It is marinated with turmeric power and boiled in water</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 150px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_3_-_saut%C3%A9eing_spices.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"Step 3: Spices (cumin, fennel, fenugreek, mustard and nigella seeds together known as poncho phutono or pancha phutana) sautéed\"><img alt=\"Step 3: Spices (cumin, fennel, fenugreek, mustard and nigella seeds together known as poncho phutono or pancha phutana) sautéed\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_3_-_saut%C3%A9eing_spices.jpg/120px-Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_3_-_saut%C3%A9eing_spices.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"109\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_3_-_saut%C3%A9eing_spices.jpg/250px-Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_3_-_saut%C3%A9eing_spices.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2448\" data-file-height=\"2230\"></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">Step 3: Spices (cumin, fennel, fenugreek, mustard and nigella seeds together known as <i>poncho phutono</i> or <i>pancha phutana</i>) sautéed</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 150px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_4_-_cooking_boiled_elephant_apple_with_spices.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"Step 4: Boiled elephant apple cooked with spices, a little bit of salt and jaggery for about five minutes\"><img alt=\"Step 4: Boiled elephant apple cooked with spices, a little bit of salt and jaggery for about five minutes\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_4_-_cooking_boiled_elephant_apple_with_spices.jpg/120px-Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_4_-_cooking_boiled_elephant_apple_with_spices.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"117\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_4_-_cooking_boiled_elephant_apple_with_spices.jpg/250px-Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_4_-_cooking_boiled_elephant_apple_with_spices.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2448\" data-file-height=\"2381\"></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">Step 4: Boiled elephant apple cooked with spices, a little bit of salt and jaggery for about five minutes</div>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 150px;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_5_-_garnishing_Ou_khota_with_ground_coconut.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" title=\"Step 5: Cooked Ou khota is garnished with ground coconut and cooked for another five minutes\"><img alt=\"Step 5: Cooked Ou khota is garnished with ground coconut and cooked for another five minutes\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_5_-_garnishing_Ou_khota_with_ground_coconut.jpg/120px-Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_5_-_garnishing_Ou_khota_with_ground_coconut.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"102\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_5_-_garnishing_Ou_khota_with_ground_coconut.jpg/250px-Ou_Khota_recipe_-_step_5_-_garnishing_Ou_khota_with_ground_coconut.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"2448\" data-file-height=\"2887\"></a></span></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">Step 5: Cooked <i>Ou khota</i> is garnished with ground coconut and cooked for another five minutes</div>\n\t\t</li>\n</ul>",
